  <div class="ts-insight-text">
    <em>Tefillin</em> = the daily channel of <em>Chayim Nitzchiyim</em>.<br>
    Each <em>moed</em> expresses a different facet of the same principle:<br><br>
    <em>Purim</em>: subduing <em>ge'us</em> (Haman) → <em>ad d'lo yada</em><br>
    <em>Pesach</em>: <em>Mochin d'Gadlus</em> out of order → <em>matzah</em><br>
    <em>Sefirah</em>: purifying the <em>Moach</em>, day by day<br>
    <em>Lag BaOmer</em>: the <em>gal</em> — partition against evil thoughts<br>
    <em>Shavuos</em>: receiving Torah = the culmination<br><br>
    All flowing from one source: <em>seeing the Tzaddik's face</em>.
  </div>
